{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And it shall be, you shall call Me 'my husband,' and you shall no longer call Me 'my master'</b> — for so is written את ימי הבעלים. And R. Marinus said: even a word that is doubtful, like בעל, which is a name of idolatry, or like כי יבעל בחור, you shall not mention anymore."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The comment addresses Hosea 2:18 (in some numbering 2:16); Ibn Ezra quotes R. Marinus on the dual sense of בעל as both 'husband/master' and as a pagan deity-name."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:54.891146230Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}